  "text": "Crop Production | UMN Extension Home Agriculture Crop production Cover crops Benefits, selection, establishment, maintenance, use and termination of cover crops. Growing forages in Minnesota Planting and growing legumes, nutrient management, pest management, harvest and storage Nutrient management Research-based nutrient management guidelines Growing small grains in Minnesota Small grains growth staging, nutrient management, variety selection, planting guidelines, harvest and storage, and pest management Growing soybean in Minnesota Soybean growth staging, nutrient management, assessing weather damage Growing sugarbeet Sugarbeet production, nutrient management and pest management Weed management for Minnesota crops Weeds commonly found in Minnesota crop production, herbicides and herbicide resistance strategies Crops current issues and highlighted resources Learn how Minnesota weather challenges affect crop management decisions. Digital Crop Doc The UMN Extension crops team can help you diagnose diseases in corn, forages, soybeans, small grains, and sugarbeet. Growing corn in Minnesota Applied research on corn production to help Minnesota farmers maximize corn yield and profitability. Regional research trials Variety trials, herbicide evaluations, other regional research © 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota. All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This work is supported by the U.S. Department of Agriculture’s National Institute of Food and Agriculture. Report Web Accessibility Issues | Privacy Statement | Staff intranet",
